WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
In the Han dynasty, the city of Chang'an awoke in golden morning light.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.140
The streets were busy with people coming and going.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:16.770
The merchants carefully loaded bundle after bundle of silk onto the camels' backs, ready to set out.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:24.910
The camel caravan entered the vast desert, walking step by step as the wind-blown sand danced around them.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:32.250
At an oasis in the desert, the caravan met merchants from Central Asia, and everyone greeted each other happily.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:38.780
They exchanged goods with one another — Han silk was traded for fine horses and all kinds of treasures.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:45.400
The Silk Road was not a single road, but like a great net connecting East and West.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:53.080
As the sun set, the fully laden caravan walked the road home — and the story of the Silk Road goes on.

